{
  "README": [
    "Golden QR matrices produced by an encoder we did not write, so that",
    "frontend/src/lib/qr/encode.ts cannot be validated against its own bugs.",
    "Rows are the bare symbol, row-major from the top-left, with no quiet zone;",
    "'1' is a dark module.",
    "Regenerate by re-running the generator named in `oracle` over `text`."
  ],
  "oracle": "python `qrcode` 8.2 (reference algorithm by Kazuhiko Arase)",
  "oracleNote": [
    "segno 1.6.6 was tried first and rejected: its write_padding_bits() uses",
    "(8 - length % 8) instead of (8 - length % 8) % 8, so whenever the bit",
    "stream already ends on a codeword boundary -- which in byte mode is every",
    "payload that has room for a full terminator -- it appends a spurious 0x00",
    "pad codeword. ISO/IEC 18004:2015 7.4.10 permits only 0xEC and 0x11 as pad",
    "codewords, and segno consequently disagrees with `qrcode` on 117 of the 123",
    "byte-mode payloads sampled. `qrcode` and encode.ts agree on all 489 payloads",
    "sampled, covering every byte length from 1 to 425."
  ],
